# Complete owned HTTP failure set

| HTTP | Code |
| --- | --- |
| 400 | `VALIDATION_FAILED` |
| 401 | `AUTH_SESSION_EXPIRED` |
| 403 | `ACCESS_DENIED` |
| 404 | `RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND` |
| 409 | `STORAGE_COMMIT_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN` |
| 503 | `STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE` |
| 503 | `STORAGE_CANCELLED` |
| 503 | `STORAGE_TIMEOUT` |
| 503 | `STORAGE_LOCK_TIMEOUT` |
| 503 | `STORAGE_DEADLOCK` |
| 503 | `STORAGE_COMMIT_ROLLED_BACK` |

No owned failure returns a data payload. Internal
SCHEDULING_QUOTA_POLICY_UNAVAILABLE and
SCHEDULING_RESERVATION_TRANSACTION_REQUIRED map to STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE.
SCHEDULING_QUOTA_UNCONFIGURED and SCHEDULING_QUOTA_UNALLOCATED are fixed
reason codes in a successful status, not HTTP failures. Their actions are
configure_quota_policy and configure_workspace_quota respectively.

Identity recheck maps revoked/disabled/demoted/source-invalid sessions to
AUTH_SESSION_EXPIRED. There are no account/source/reauthentication-specific
codes in this module. Unknown owner errors are not forwarded.

This table covers the actual Handle boundary, after IAM authentication.
IAM must retain and enumerate its own actual pre-dispatch authentication,
origin, readiness and capacity errors using its existing problem catalog.
The review schema intentionally does not invent a complete IAM error list.
